Carafe Lab: d3d12 offers GL_EXT_shader_image_load_formatted when the GPU loads every format from a typed UAV, which is
the condition it already requires for shader images. A DXIL typed load takes its format from the view, so a load with
no format in the shader needs nothing more. Without the extension, Eden's OpenGL renderer could not compile guest
compute shaders that load images with no format (NVK's), and their dispatches ran no shader at all.
MIT, as the file it changes.

--- a/src/gallium/drivers/d3d12/d3d12_screen.cpp
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/d3d12/d3d12_screen.cpp
@@ -346,6 +346,7 @@
    caps->query_timestamp = true;
    caps->vertex_element_instance_divisor = true;
    caps->image_store_formatted = true;
+   caps->image_load_formatted = screen->support_shader_images;
    caps->glsl_tess_levels_as_inputs = true;

    caps->max_stream_output_buffers = D3D12_SO_BUFFER_SLOT_COUNT;
